[31m-Workshop learning checkpoint. Local demo; no login or multi-user isolation.[m
[32m+[m[32mA hands-on web app development workshop project. It adds, displays, edits and deletes engineering projects, with data stored in local SQLite.[m
 [m
[31m-## Run[m
[31m-Use Node.js 22.23.3 (tested baseline) and a PowerShell terminal in this folder.[m
[32m+[m[32m## Run locally[m
[32m+[m[32mUse the workshop Node 22 baseline (at least 22.18, below 23), Git and VS Code.[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen a PowerShell terminal inside the project, then run:[m
 [m
[31m-```powershell[m
[31m-npm.cmd install[m
[31m-npm.cmd start[m
[31m-```[m
[32m+[m[32m    npm.cmd ci[m
[32m+[m[32m    npm.cmd start[m
 [m
[31m-Open http://localhost:3000. Keep the server terminal running. Stop with Ctrl+C.[m
[31m-The pinned versions and lockfile are supplied in the released kit. After the first install, use `npm.cmd ci` when restoring dependencies.[m
[32m+[m[32mOpen http://localhost:3000. Stop the server with Ctrl+C.[m
 [m
[31m-## Files[m
[31m-`public/index.html`: structure; `public/style.css`: presentation; `public/script.js`: browser behaviour.[m
[31m-`server.js`: local startup. When present, `app.js`: HTTP API; `database.js`: persistence.[m
[32m+[m[32m## How it works[m
[32m+[m[32mBrowser HTML/CSS/JavaScript -> fetch/HTTP -> Express API -> SQLite -> JSON response -> updated page.[m
[32m+[m[32m- public/index.html: page structure and form.[m
[32m+[m[32m- public/style.css: appearance and responsive layout.[m
[32m+[m[32m- public/script.js: input, API requests, rendering and feedback.[m
[32m+[m[32m- server.js: starts the local server.[m
[32m+[m[32m- app.js: routes, validation and responses.[m
[32m+[m[32m- database.js: SQLite operations; creates data/projects.db locally.[m
 [m
[31m-## Evidence[m
[31m-Explain the current storage location and what survives browser refresh and server restart.[m
[31m-For the final checkpoint, run `npm.cmd test` to verify CRUD, validation and persistence.[m
[31m-Local browser data is not automatically migrated to SQLite. Recreate test records after switching.[m
[32m+[m[32m## API[m
[32m+[m[32mGET /api/health; GET and POST /api/projects; PUT and DELETE /api/projects/:id.[m
 [m
[31m-## GitHub[m
[31m-Commit source code and package-lock.json. Exclude node_modules, data and credentials.[m
[31m-Describe your own project and add evidence of testing to this README before the final push.[m
[32m+[m[32m## Verification[m
[32m+[m[32mRecord only checks actually performed: [add your CRUD, restart, failure/retry and mobile test results here].[m
[32m+[m[32mIf the supplied test/crud.test.js is present, run npm.cmd test. It tests the reference API using a temporary database, not browser interactions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Workshop limitations[m
[32m+[m[32mThis local teaching app has no sign-in or per-user permissions. Browsers calling the same server share its collection. The SQLite data file and node_modules are not uploaded to GitHub. Cloud hosting requires separate server and database configuration.[m
